---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---
<Site
  title="About · Ouijit"
  description="Ouijit is built by one person, Prentice Bjerkeseth. Free, open source under AGPL, no account and no telemetry, and the plan is to keep it that way.">
  <main class="compare-content about-content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      A tool for working with coding agents shouldn't need an account, a subscription, or a company behind it.
      It should be made with care. And as you get more done with it, it should protect your attention and
      your care for the work, not consume them. That is what I'm trying to build.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ouijit runs the agents' own CLIs in real terminals rather than standing in for them, because the
      command line is where their tooling moves fastest.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ouijit has no account and no telemetry. You shouldn't have to log in to use a tool like this, and you
      shouldn't have to give up privacy to get a good one. The only usage number I have is how many times the
      builds have been downloaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ouijit is free and open source under AGPL-3.0. If it ever charges for something, it will be a feature
      that costs me something to run, like hosted environments or sync. The app itself stays free.
    </p>
    <p>
      Many tools like this are raising venture money, getting acquired, or shutting down. I build Ouijit
      alone, and I want it to still be standing, still free and still private.
    </p>
    <p class="about-sign"><a href="https://github.com/pbjer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prentice Bjerkeseth</a></p>
  </main>
</Site>
